<body>
    <h1>Future Scope</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"FutureScope-BusinessRequirements">Business Requirements</=
h1>
<p><strong>Scenario 1: PM sub-advisors who are our client </strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>Users will be set under their =E2=80=98primary firm=E2=80=99 and linke=
d to the firms of their sub-advising accounts as their =E2=80=98secondary f=
irm(s)=E2=80=99</li>
 <li>Users only have limited Account feature access on their sub-advising a=
ccounts</li>
 <li>Users must have trading capability and be able to do individual trade =
orders, trade allocation and basket booking on their primary accounts and s=
ub-advising accounts on the same view - &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"mailto:joseph.kim@nbc.ca" rel=3D"nofollow">@Kim, Joseph</a> This is r=
eferred as the =E2=80=98aggregated=E2=80=99 view of Order module. Owen and =
I can update you about this.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scenario 2: Parent group concept</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>Examples: (1) Rae &amp; Lipskie =E2=80=93 All child firms inherit the =
same CX firm settings as the parent, (2) Cumberland =E2=80=93 Not all the s=
ame.</li>
 <li>CX must load the parent-child relation and which child firms share the=
 CX firm settings as the parent from Firm360.</li>
 <li>Users assigned to different child firms which inherit the firm setting=
s of the parent would have the same entitlement settings (per user group) a=
nd be able to access accounts across firm ranges (subject to RR code assign=
ment), basically, functioning as one firm.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Scenario 3: PM sub-advisors who are not our client</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>Users will be set under the firm of their sub-advising accounts for wh=
ite-labelling and firm-specific settings</li>
 <li>However, they must only have limited Account feature access on their s=
ub-advising accounts but full trading capability.</li>
 <li><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"mailto:varun.anand@nbc.ca" rel=3D"n=
ofollow">@Anand, Varun</a> Question - Though this user has one firm only, I=
 think the =E2=80=98assignment type=E2=80=99 should be marked as =E2=80=98S=
=E2=80=99 to indicate that their assigned RR code ranges are =E2=80=98PM su=
b-advisory RR codes=E2=80=99 (as opposed to primary rr codes). What do you =
think? Thanks.</li>
</ul>
    </div>
</body>
